    },
    {
      "passage_id": "susie_hears_1",
      "clause_idx": 2,
      "text": "\"What are you crying for?\" Susie asked.",
      "n_mentions": 3,
      "argmax_token": "Susie"
    },
    {
      "passage_id": "susie_helps_2",
      "clause_idx": 0,
      "text": "Then Susie took the little girl into the house.",
      "n_mentions": 3,
      "argmax_token": "house"
    },
    {
      "passage_id": "susie_helps_2",
      "clause_idx": 1,
      "text": "She cheered her up with kind words, and gave her a nice dress and a pair of shoes.",
      "n_mentions": 8,
      "argmax_token": "shoes"
    },
    {
      "passage_id": "susie_helps_2",
      "clause_idx": 2,
      "text": "This brought real joy and gladness to the poor child, and she, too, thought that Susie was rightly called Sunbeam.",
      "n_mentions": 7,
      "argmax_token": "Sunbeam"
    },
    {
      "passage_id": "mary_dash_doll",
      "clause_idx": 0,
      "text": "Mary ran about and played with Dash, her pet dog, and was having a happy time.",
      "n_mentions": 6,
      "argmax_token": "time"
    },
    {
      "passage_id": "mary_dash_doll",
      "clause_idx": 1,
      "text": "But in a corner of the yard she found her nicest doll all torn and broken, and its dress covered with mud.",
      "n_mentions": 8,
      "argmax_token": "mud"
    },
    {
      "passage_id": "mary_dash_doll",
      "clause_idx": 2,
      "text": "She knew, at once, that Dash had done this, and she scolded him harshly.",
      "n_mentions": 5,
      "argmax_token": "him"
    },
    {
      "passage_id": "harry_carriage",
      "clause_idx": 0,
      "text": "Soon after, a fine carriage came up, and in it were Harry and his mother.",
      "n_mentions": 5,
      "argmax_token": "Harry"
    },
    {
      "passage_id": "harry_carriage",
      "clause_idx": 1,
      "text": "The blind man stood, and held out his hat.",
      "n_mentions": 4,
      "argmax_token": "hat"
    },
    {
      "passage_id": "harry_carriage",
      "clause_idx": 2,
      "text": "\"Let us give the poor man something,\" said Harry to his mother.",
      "n_mentions": 6,
      "argmax_token": "Harry"
    },
    {
      "passage_id": "edgar_thomas_boat",
      "clause_idx": 0,
      "text": "\"Keep still, please, young gentlemen,\" said the boatman, when Edgar Rose and Thomas Read began to move from one side to the other.",
      "n_mentions": 7,
      "argmax_token": "boatman"
    },
    {
      "passage_id": "edgar_thomas_boat",
      "clause_idx": 1,
      "text": "They kept quiet for a short time only.",
      "n_mentions": 2,
      "argmax_token": "time"
    },
    {
      "passage_id": "edgar_thomas_boat",
      "clause_idx": 2,
      "text": "Edgar soon wanted a stick which Thomas held in his hand.",
      "n_mentions": 6,
      "argmax_token": "hand"
    },
    {
      "passage_id": "james_sport_dog",
      "clause_idx": 0,
      "text": "Sport is a good watchdog, and a kind playfellow.",
      "n_mentions": 4,
      "argmax_token": "playfellow"
    },
    {
      "passage_id": "james_sport_dog",
      "clause_idx": 1,
      "text": "Every night he guards the house while James and his father are asleep.",
      "n_mentions": 6,
      "argmax_token": "father"
    },
    {
      "passage_id": "james_sport_dog",
      "clause_idx": 2,
      "text": "In the daytime, James often uses Sport for his horse.",
      "n_mentions": 5,
      "argmax_token": "horse"
    }
  ],
